  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seed Sector Study</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to assess the performance of the seed sector in C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire, with a special focus on African eggplant, Amaranth, Onion, Okra, Pepper, Potato and Tomato. The key objectives are: 1.	To get a better understanding of the seed sector performance, both formal and informal, with a focus on the abovementioned crops. The performance of the seed sector should amongst others include attention for the regulatory and institutional environment, as well as market dynamics such as access to quality seeds, import balance, overview of all relevant actors, and challenges and opportunities surrounding the effects of climate change. 2.	To identify key constraints in the seed sector that affect all relevant actors 3.	To create stakeholder alignment and identify possibilities for partnerships and collaborations with Ivorian-Dutch stakeholders, both public and private, and to create alignment on how to tackle the key constraints, in combination with the identification of possible interventions and recommendations for seed sector development. 4.	This study will be the starting point for a seed sector roadmap and wider seed sector development programming, both from the Dutch ministry of Foreign affairs and the HortiNord combitrack.</narrative>
  </description>
